
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relations.mgr - Japanese-pack kinship + attribute relations (Phase 8).
#
# Each entry maps a Japanese term to the canonical (English) ontology label.
# Labels are language-neutral; only the surface text differs by pack.
#
# Two cuts to flag for the next agent:
#
#   1) Japanese splits sibling-by-birth-order: 兄 / 弟 (elder / younger
#      brother), 姉 / 妹 (elder / younger sister). English's brother / sister
#      labels carry no birth-order, so a player who types 弟 vs 兄 gets the
#      same belief written either way. Generation default is the honorific
#      form (兄, 姉) - elder is the most common kinship assumption when
#      birth-order is unknown. A future /birth_order aux on kinship beliefs
#      would let the realizer pick correctly; see dialogue_nlg_phase8_design.md
#      section 8.10.
#
#   2) お母さん / お父さん (polite forms used when addressing someone else's
#      family) are accepted on parse but generation v1 defaults to the
#      neutral 母 / 父. Sonkeigo / kenjougo would split these properly; v1's
#      two-tier keigo (plain vs polite) rides intent tags on the Statements
#      templates, not on the REL lookups.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:PASSIVE_PNAME_REL
"の 名前 は"            /pres name              .
"の 名前 は"            /past name              .


:PASSIVE_NUM_REL
"の 年齢 は"            /past age               .


:PASSIVE_REL
"の $rel(REL) は"       /pres $rel(REL)         .
"の $rel(REL) は"       /past $rel(REL)         .


:RELP
"兄弟"                  sibling                 .
"親"                    parent                  .
"兄たち"                 brother                 .
"姉たち"                 sister                  .
"子供 たち"             child                   .
"いとこ たち"            cousin                  .
"友達 たち"             friend                   .
"隣人 たち"             neighbour               .


